      "headline": "Vice President, Engineering, Unreal Engine",
      "about": "I am an industry veteran with 30 years in real-time software development. I have spent the last 20 years in the video game industry and helped to establish Epic's Montreal Studio. I am passionate about crafting tools and workflows that empower creators to bring their visions to life. As Epic Games’ Vice-President of Engineering for Unreal Engine, I have the opportunity to lead the amazing team behind Unreal Engine. I am  dedicated to the UE team's innovation and focus on quality and user experience. Prior to Epic, I led the development of iconic AAA Ubisoft titles such as Splinter Cell and Assassin's Creed.\n\nIn my role, I've been focusing on improving vision alignment, team efficiency and structure, and delivering breakthrough technologies in a fast moving environment.\n\nMy leadership style revolves around cultivating robust and efficient teams and ensuring each member performs at their pinnacle. What sets me apart is my keen ability to identify talent, fostering their growth through tailored coaching and mentorship.",
